  "id": "COMPOUND:28772 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, mediated through Caspase-5. This pathway involves a series of molecular interactions where the former acts as a target for multiple compounds, including a phenolic compound and a fatty acid derivative, all of which ultimately target the latter enzyme. The consistent presence of Caspase-5 as a central node in the target hierarchy indicates a potential mechanism of action involving caspase activation or regulation. The evidence supports the idea that the compound of interest may exert its effects by modulating Caspase-5, which in turn influences the activity of the SDR family member 9. The overlapping targets and the shared role of Caspase-5 in the pathway suggest a possible functional link, though the exact mechanism of how the compound interacts with Caspase-5 remains to be elucidated.",
